# Ava identity — posts

When the user asks Ava to say something on Slack or Discord:

## Slack (hard)

- **Never** use Cursor Slack MCP (`plugin-slack-slack` / `slack_send_message`) for Ava messages. That posts as the **operator’s workspace login** (Alex), not Ava.
- **Always** post with `AVA_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` via:
  - `Web Files/rootmc-ava/src/avaPost.mjs` → `postAvaSlack`
  - or `node Web Files/rootmc-ava/scripts/post-as-ava.mjs slack <channelId> [thread_ts]`
- Confirm the resulting message author is Ava (`U0BMBNYPYA2`), not Alex (`U0BLWBTGYTU`).

## Discord

- Use `AVA_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN` via `postAvaDiscord` / `scripts/post-as-ava.mjs discord <channelId> [messageId]`.
- Never post as RootMC Official or any other bot unless the user asks for that bot by name.

## Do not

- Soft-pedal “shared tool / fingerprints” if a post landed under Alex — admit it and re-post as Ava if needed.
- Use Slack MCP “for convenience” for Ava voice.
